Quoted from http://www.steelypips.org/nethack/elbereth_faq.html:

"Writing in the dust. This can be with your finger, a soft gem, a ring
without a hard gem, any charged wand except digging, fire, or
lightning, and so forth. Note that you have a 1/25 chance of screwing
up each letter if you're engraving in the dust. While this only takes
one turn, any movement-like fighting-on your part will smudge it out.
Even staying put will erode it, since no-one stands perfectly still.
In other words, if you write in the dust, you can't expect it to last
very long. However, the higher your dexterity is, the more slowly it
will smudge. You can also avoid smudging completely by levitation over
the writing in the dust."

Assuming you aren't blind/confused/stunned/hallucinating, you have a
(24/25)^8 = 72% chance of correctly writing Elbereth in the dust.
However, your dexterity affects if the writing will smudge, even if
you aren't moving at all.  This also means that writing Elbereth 4
times in a row is affected by your dexterity, because it takes more
than one turn to write Elbereth 4 times, which means that writing
Elbereth multiple times in itself has a chance to smudge the letters
you are writing in the dust.  This is why writing Elbereth 4 times in
a row isn't a 99% success rate when you actually try this in the game.



